---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const threads = [
  {
    key: "search",
    label: "Search surface",
    tension: "People needed to move from uncertain policy questions to useful records quickly.",
    owned: "Built search and result surfaces for policy, journal, and transitional-agreement discovery.",
    proof: "Search became the main path through a complex compliance dataset.",
  },
  {
    key: "docs",
    label: "Help and documentation",
    tension: "The product needed to serve institutional users, API consumers, and internal stakeholders.",
    owned: "Built help pages and documentation surfaces around product and API understanding.",
    proof: "Support material lived closer to the product surface it explained.",
  },
  {
    key: "data",
    label: "Source data quality",
    tension: "Search trust depended on records staying clear, aligned, and explainable.",
    owned: "Supported indexing, data-pipeline feedback, and source-data quality loops.",
    proof: "Policy and journal records became easier to keep aligned with the search experience.",
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Open Policy Finder - Owen Abel Amenze"
  description="A case note on Open Policy Finder work across search, documentation, and data quality."
>
  <article class="case-note" data-case-note>
    <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/work">Work</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span>Open Policy Finder</span>
    </nav>

    <header class="case-hero">
      <p class="eyebrow">Case note</p>
      <h1>Open Policy Finder</h1>
      <p>
        Work on a Jisc product surface where open access compliance depended on
        policy, journal, and transitional-agreement data being searchable,
        legible, and trusted.
      </p>
    </header>

    <dl class="case-meta" aria-label="Case note summary">
      <div>
        <dt>Context</dt>
        <dd>Jisc / 2023-26</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Focus</dt>
        <dd>Search, help, documentation, indexing, data quality</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Link</dt>
        <dd>
          <a href="https://openpolicyfinder.jisc.ac.uk">openpolicyfinder.jisc.ac.uk</a>
        </dd>
      </div>
    </dl>

    <section class="case-section" aria-labelledby="case-tension">
      <h2 id="case-tension">Tension</h2>
      <p>
        Open access compliance is practical work. Users arrive with specific
        questions about policies, journals, agreements, and eligibility, and the
        interface has to help them move through that uncertainty without hiding
        the shape of the underlying data.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="case-section" aria-labelledby="case-threads">
      <h2 id="case-threads">Threads</h2>
      <div class="case-thread-grid">
        {
          threads.map((thread) => (
            <button class="case-thread" type="button" data-thread={thread.key} aria-pressed="false">
              <span>{thread.label}</span>
              <small>{thread.tension}</small>
            </button>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="case-section" aria-labelledby="case-owned">
      <h2 id="case-owned">Owned</h2>
      <table class="case-ledger">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Thread</th>
            <th scope="col">Work</th>
            <th scope="col">Signal</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {
            threads.map((thread) => (
              <tr data-thread={thread.key}>
                <td>{thread.label}</td>
                <td>{thread.owned}</td>
                <td>{thread.proof}</td>
              </tr>
            ))
          }
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </section>

    <section class="case-section case-flow" aria-labelledby="case-shape">
      <h2 id="case-shape">Shape</h2>
      <ol>
        <li data-thread="search">A user starts with a policy or journal question.</li>
        <li data-thread="search">The search surface narrows the problem into inspectable results.</li>
        <li data-thread="docs">Help and documentation explain how to interpret the product surface.</li>
        <li data-thread="data">Source-data feedback keeps the search experience aligned with the records.</li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="case-section" aria-labelledby="case-note">
      <h2 id="case-note">Note</h2>
      <p>
        The important part was not only building a search page. It was making a
        compliance surface easier to operate and easier to trust, from the
        public interface through to the data and documentation around it.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>

  <script>
    const caseNote = document.querySelector("[data-case-note]");
    const controls = caseNote.querySelectorAll(".case-thread[data-thread]");
    const related = caseNote.querySelectorAll("[data-thread]");

    const setThread = (key) => {
      const nextKey = caseNote.dataset.activeThread === key ? undefined : key;
      caseNote.dataset.activeThread = nextKey ?? "";

      related.forEach((node) => {
        const active = Boolean(nextKey) && node.dataset.thread === nextKey;
        node.toggleAttribute("data-active", active);

        if (node.matches(".case-thread")) {
          node.setAttribute("aria-pressed", String(active));
        }
      });
    };

    controls.forEach((control) => {
      control.addEventListener("click", () => setThread(control.dataset.thread));
    });

    document.addEventListener("keydown", (event) => {
      if (event.key === "Escape") {
        setThread(caseNote.dataset.activeThread);
      }
    });
  </script>
</BaseLayout>
